    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0531" n="407" xml:id="pg407"/>

                <head>No. 231.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Noyes</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 23,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 363.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information a
                    copy of a letter to this Department from the firm of S. Davis, jr., &amp; Co.,
                    making some statements in regard to the proceedings of the French authorities in
                    reference to certain lots of pork sent to France by them for sale.</p>
                <p>In view of the great hardships to which this firm have been exposed by the action
                    of the French Government, based upon false reports as to an extraordinary
                    prevalence of trichinosis among the hogs of this country, I will thank you to
                    bring the complaints of Messrs. S. Davis, jr., &amp; Co. to the attention of the
                    French foreign office with a view of obtaining for them such relief as may be
                    practicable.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d235-a1.xml" xpointer="d235-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
